hey guys so this video will admittedly  be something completely different today  because i want to introduce you guys to  a new series that i've discovered this  week  and also discuss its latest chapter a  little bit the series i'm talking about  is  kaiju number eight i stumbled across it  when looking for a new series to start  on manga plus  and it's actually listed as the eighth  most popular series there at the moment  even before the likes of chainsaw man or  jujutsu kaisen  and since there are only nine chapters  so far and the cover art looks pretty  damn awesome  i figured i'd give it a go and holy [ __ ]  what a story it is if you want to start  reading before watching this video  all 9 chapters are free to read so far  and the link is in the description below  just make sure to come back afterwards  there are a number of familiar concepts  in here that we already know from other  manga  but so far that really doesn't seem to  be a bad thing at all  just the opposite really the series  written and illustrated by narya  matsumoto  takes place in modern day tokyo the only  difference is that for some  still unknown reason enormous monsters  pop up to harass the people at times  threatening civilization to counter this  the country has created the so-called  defense force  which sole purpose is to destroy these  enormous creatures  the strongest member is mina ashiro a  tough looking woman that we see destroy  one of these gigantrous beasts with  relative ease  up to this point the story carries some  aspects of both attack on titan  as well as pacific rim however kaiju  number 8 addresses an issue that most  giant monster stories gloss over  what happens once these beasts have been  killed  this is where the main character of the  story comes into play  the 32 year old kafka whose name is  drawn from the 20th century author franz  kafka  dreamed of joining the defense force but  has failed to pass the entrance exam  multiple times and has given up on his  dream  kafka was childhood friends with mina  the two made a vow to join the defense  force and protect japan from the kaiju  together  after seeing their own town destroyed  after  failing to follow mina however he has  joined the so-called kaiju cleanup corps  instead  his job as a monster sweeper is to chop  up and dispose of kaiju killed by the  defense force  and so for a change we actually learn  about the nasty side of killing large  creatures in a civilian area  and how to clean up the mess they leave  however  everything once again changes for kafka  when the ambitious 18 year old ichikawa  is assigned to work with kafka  ichikawa also has plans to take the exam  to become a member of the defense force  and with his strong determination  manages to ignite kafka's will once  again  after being attacked by a so-called yoju  smaller monsters that accompany the main  kaiju when they emerge  both kafka and ichikawa stand their  ground but end up in the hospital  there kafka is infected by a small  parasite-like monster  and suddenly his body transforms into a  small but  quite powerful monster himself when  another kaiju appears in the city  he defeats it with ease and is from here  on out known as kaiju number 8  wanted by the public this is of course a  reference to franz kafka's story the  metamorphosis  where the main character one day wakes  up transformed into a giant insect  from here on out kafka learns to control  his new powers at will  and with his newfound strength he and  ichigawa participate in the next  entrance exam  here they meet kikoro shinomiya kikoro  is the daughter of the defense force  commander and her combat power is  far greater than any of the other  applicants she is viewed as the hope for  japan and the future leader of the  defense force  but suffers heavily under her father's  high expectations  during the exam she easily disposes of  the smaller monsters that have been set  as obstacles  similar to the entrance exam in my hero  academia  kikoru defeats most of them including  the main monster in a short amount of  time  however suddenly a mysterious humanoid  kaiju  similar to kafka's own transformation  appears who  revives the monster and gives it a power  up  quickly it defeats kikoru and threatens  to kill her  but in the last moment kafka decides to  reveal his true power in front of her  and takes out the monster with ease in  the latest chapter  we see the aftermath of the fight and  learned that the mysterious monster has  infiltrated the monster sweeper force  by taking up human appearances now  obviously should i decide to keep going  with this series i will make the chapter  reviews much much more thoroughly  however since this is the very first  video on this and most of you probably  have just heard about the story for the  very first time  i prefer to share with you guys why i  have such high hopes for this manga  despite sharing elements with other  popular stories i believe that up to  this point  all of them have been presented in a  quite unique and interesting way  the fact that so little is explained  about the world and how these creatures  came to be in the first place  hint at something larger being at work  here and it feels like this story might  have  quite a bunch of things to be revealed  and explored over time  promising some great world building no  pun  intended in this sense it gives me great  attack on titan vibes as well  but in a more than positive way the art  style is also really nice  reminding me at times of both boku no  hero and  fire force most importantly for me  however the characters  all seem to be more than promising as in  the handful of chapters we've gotten so  far  there's already a lot happening in terms  of characterization  and shaping complex personalities  in addition to the excellent action good  plotting and pacing and quality  character work  matsumoto also delivers some wonderful  comedy  the body team of kafka and ichigawa have  created some excellent chemistry between  the different characters in a super  short amount of time  the story also promises to have a great  balance between some fun shonen vibes  and some  darker and more mature elements which i  personally am a big fan of  many of the panels are flat out  wonderful to look at  all of them are meticulously drawn and  the action is kinetic  and leaps out of the page facial  expressions and emotions are  also wonderfully captured combined with  great writing and a good balance between  inner and outer dialogue  every chapter so far has really captured  me completely  and so overall kaiju number 8 is a  brilliant and fun read  that delivers great chapter after great  chapter  getting me excited for the next one  while it's still way too early to make  any predictions  i think that the story has enormous  potential and i highly recommend  checking it out  you will definitely not be disappointed  and once you've done so please let me  know if this is something you would like  me to cover on a weekly basis  because it really depends on your  feedback and preference  so make sure to share your thoughts on  this with me in the comments below  thanks guys peace  you
 

